From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chris McLaughlin <19711592+qBitnaut@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 12:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] SL7 local: dt-bindings: clock: qcom,x1e80100-camcc: Allow the
 display GDSC as a third power domain

The previous patch lists the display MDSS_GDSC as a third power domain
of the camera clock controller, so the display GDSC is on while the
camera runs. The schema allows exactly two power domains, so dtbs_check
rejects the romulus device trees with "power-domains: [...] is too
long".

Accept a third, optional power domain. required-opps stays at two
entries: it describes the performance points of the MXC and MMCX
domains by index, and the GDSC has none.

Origin: omarchy-dragon-sl7 (companion to the preceding patch, from Omarchy linux-omarchy-aarch64 2207)
Upstream-Status: Not submitted (2207 itself is not upstream)

---
 Documentation/devicetree/bindings/clock/qcom,x1e80100-camcc.yaml | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/clock/qcom,x1e80100-camcc.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/clock/qcom,x1e80100-camcc.yaml
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/clock/qcom,x1e80100-camcc.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/clock/qcom,x1e80100-camcc.yaml
@@ -36,9 +36,13 @@
       - description: Sleep clock source
 
   power-domains:
+    minItems: 2
     items:
       - description: A phandle to the MXC power-domain
       - description: A phandle to the MMCX power-domain
+      - description:
+          A phandle to the display MDSS GDSC, held on while the camera runs
+          (optional, required-opps covers the first two domains only)
 
   required-opps:
     items:
